   `/api/settings`. Events: `handoff {text}` on a child's last run, `round_finished {round, notes, completed}` on a round.
 
+## API tokens
+- Personal tokens (`aht_` + 43 url-safe chars) authenticate `/api/*` (not `/api/auth/*`) with `Authorization: Bearer <token>` instead of the session cookie. A token acts as its user in the workspace it was created in; it does not follow workspace switches.
+- Scopes: `read` allows GET/HEAD only (any other method is a 403 before routing), `write` allows everything the user can do except managing tokens (`/api/tokens` needs a session).
+- Only the sha256 of the secret is stored, plus its first 8 chars for display. The secret is returned once, by `POST /api/tokens`. Expired, revoked or unknown tokens, and tokens of users who left the workspace, are a 401; an Authorization header is never mixed with the cookie.
+- `last_used_at` is updated whenever a request authenticates with the token. A token may make 100 requests per minute (429 with `Retry-After` beyond that; sessions are not limited), and a user has at most 20 tokens per workspace.
+
 ## Guardrails
 
 - `tests/` and `evals/` are read-only to agents (harness rejects writes).
